// Smart Money Concepts [v15.4]
// Based on v12.2 — (c) LuxAlgo CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
// v12   — Pivot Source toggle, OB tolerance >2, Liquidity Sweeps
// v12.1 — Trailing extreme fix (strict >/< ), simultaneous cross safe silence
// v12.2 — Breaker Blocks (mitigated OBs convert with flipped bias)
// v13.0 — Kill Zones, Session Boxes, Previous Day/Week Levels
// v13.1 — MSS, Displacement Candles, Asian Range
// v14.0 — OTE Zone, OB Touch Count, iFVG, NDOG/NWOG, CE Midlines (OB/BB)
// v14.1 — iFVG static boxes, NDOG confirmed mitigation, OB text clear fix, touch bar skip, weekly security merge
// v14.2 — NDOG age expiry (hours-based), NDOG/NWOG confirmed-bar creation, FVG/iFVG CE lines removed, NWOG never age-expires
// v15.0 — FVG duplication fix, OTE degenerate cleanup, Asian range reset fix, Midnight Open, Silver Bullet windows
// v15.1 — OB touch count edge-detection fix (outside→inside transition only)
// v15.2 — OB touch count: wasInside default flipped to TRUE so the OB candle
//         and its immediate follow-through are no longer miscounted as "1x".
//         Touch detection now reuses the SAME mitigation source predicate that
//         deleteOrderBlocks() uses, keeping touch counting and OB removal in
//         sync under both CLOSE and HIGH/LOW mitigation modes. Breaker
//         conversion seeds wasInside = true to avoid phantom 1x on flip.
// v15.3 — Verified bug-fix release:
//         • Bearish OTE zone now anchored from swing bottom (premium half) — was
//           previously drawn in the discount half regardless of trend direction.
//           Same fix applied to the OTE-touch alert at the bottom of the script.
//         • OTE zone is no longer drawn before the first BOS/CHoCH (bias == 0).
//         • updateTrailingExtremes() now honours `pivotSourceInput` (Wick vs
//           Body), keeping Strong/Weak H/L, Premium/Discount, and OTE consistent
//           with swing pivot detection.
//         • leg() guards bars where `bar_index < 2 * size` to prevent vacuous
//           left-side pivot confirmation on the first warm-up bars.
//         • storeOrderBlock() now back-fills `touchCount` for the historical gap
//           between the OB candle (parsedIndex) and the detection bar, so the
//           first user-visible "1x" reflects real retests, not the first
//           post-detection retest.
//         • Breaker Blocks now have full touch counting (parity with OBs) via
//           updateBreakerBlockTouches(); BB creation bar is skipped to avoid
//           phantom-mitigation gap-death immediately after conversion.
//         • PDH / PDL alerts now latch on first touch (edge-detected with [1]),
//           matching the Asian/London/NY-range alert style.
//         • Float equality on pivot snap levels replaced with mintick tolerance.
//         • barDeltaPercent corrected from delta/(open*100) to delta/open*100.
//         • htfBarDuration request.security() switched to lookahead_off.
// v15.4 — Remaining bug-fix release:
//         • OB execution order: deleteOrderBlocks() now runs BEFORE
//           updateOrderBlockTouches(). Previously, on the bar of mitigation
//           an OB could be exhausted by touch counting before
//           deleteOrderBlocks() had a chance to convert it to a BB.
//         • getStyle() now has a default branch returning line.style_solid,
//           preventing na returns on unmatched strings.
//         • `varip` currentBarIndex/lastBarIndex initialised to -1 so that
//           newBar is correctly true on the first realtime bar.
//         • BB touch count display now has its own toggle
//           (showBBTouchCountInput), separate from OB touch count.
//         • New 'Body' OB mitigation mode (now the default). Under the old
//           'High/Low' mode, a 1-tick wick above an OB level triggered
//           mitigation — in ICT terms that is a liquidity sweep, not a
//           proper mitigation. 'Body' requires math.max(open,close) to clear
//           the bearish OB top / math.min(open,close) to clear the bullish
//           OB bottom, filtering micro-wick false mitigations.
// v16.0 — Major fix release:
//         • FVG body-based mitigation fixes wick false-mitigations.
//         • BB mitigation execution order fixed to allow alerts.
//         • Timezones separated for ranges.
//         • Min penetration ticks instead of pips.
//         • iFVG creation guard prevents instant deletion.
// v16.5 — Fixes OB/BB min-penetration touch parity, BB immediate gap-through
//         guard, MSS offset markers, MSS/CHoCH double alerts, range touch alert
//         timing, stale OB/BB text, first-bar division guards, independent iFVG
//         mitigation, and hidden FVG tracking for iFVG-only mode.
// v16.6 — Replaces MSS displacement plotshape offset markers with label markers
//         so the script stays below TradingView's 64-plot hard limit.
// v20.16 — CVD÷ divergence label size is now an input (cvdDivLabelSizeInput,
//          Tiny/Small/Normal/Large/Huge, default Small — was hardcoded Tiny).
//          Applies to both the bearish and bullish on-chart divergence
//          markers. (Distinct from the v20.13 CVD status-TABLE size input.)
// v20.15 — Three more audit fixes (#2 partial, #6, #10):
//          • [#2] OB FVG-confluence now requires DIRECTIONAL alignment — a
//            bullish OB only scores the FVG point on a bullish (gap-up) 3-bar
//            FVG, a bearish OB only on a bearish (gap-down) one. Pre-v20.15
//            any gap in either direction scored it.
//          • [#6] "Opening Gap Formed" alert's NWOG portion is now keyed on a
//            new nwogFormedThisBar latch set at actual gap creation, so in
//            ICT NY anchor mode the alert fires in sync with the drawn gap
//            (Fri/Sun NY boundary) instead of always using the TV-week
//            condition. NDOG portion unchanged.
//          • [#10] EQ tolerance comparison changed from `<` to `<=` at all
//            three sites (two detection branches + pool helper). With a
//            nonzero threshold the boundary case is measure-zero so behavior
//            is unchanged, but threshold=0 (user zeros both ATR factor and
//            tick floor) now means EXACT-match instead of "never matches".
//          Same-pass findings NOT changed: #1 RVOL window (false — break bar
//          IS current bar), #3 quality permanent-miss (opt-in semantic,
//          default off), #4 breaker gap-through (persistent gap-over deletion
//          is defensible), #5 same-bar sweep (impossible by pivot validation),
//          #7 OTE freeze (fixed v20.14), #8 range-alert TF guard (already
//          double-protected), #9 EQ stale anchor (debatable, default-off).
// v20.14 — OTE Impulse-Leg freeze now triggers on first WICK touch (audit #6).
//          Pre-v20.14 the leg froze only when a bar CLOSED inside the OTE
//          band; a sharp wick into OTE that rejected without closing inside
//          (the classic first reaction) left the leg extending and the zone
//          drifting away from the actionable touch. Freeze now fires when the
//          bar's range first overlaps the band, capturing that first wick.
//          A new captureBar field on the oteLeg UDT excludes the BOS bar
//          itself, so a large displacement candle's lower wick can't freeze
//          a truncated leg on bar 0.
//          Other 7 findings from the same audit pass verified NOT actionable:
//          #1 bearish FVG .bottom (correct — far edge, documented),
//          #2 OB RVOL window (correct — storeOrderBlock runs ON the break bar
//             so size()-1 IS the break bar),
//          #3 OB session tag fixed-NY (intentional — ICT sessions are
//             NY-defined; minor cosmetic mismatch vs per-local boxes),
//          #4 quality filter mutates bias (intentional v20.1 design,
//             default-off),
//          #5 same-bar sweep of fresh pivot (impossible — pivot validation
//             guarantees the confirmation bar is inside the prior extreme),
//          #7 AVWAP tagged on moving line (natural per-bar touch test),
//          #8 range alerts lack TF guard (already double-protected by the
//             not-active and not-na predicates → can't fire on daily+).
// v20.13 — UX: readable OB confluence badge + sizable CVD table.
//          • OB confluence badge now spells out WHICH confluences scored.
//            New confluenceTag field on the orderBlock UDT, built at
//            creation from the component bools (R = institutional RVOL,
//            F = FVG overlap, P = Premium/Discount zone) and inherited on
//            Breaker conversion. The box label shows e.g. "★2 RF" instead
//            of a bare "★2", so you can read what's behind the score at a
//            glance. Tooltip updated with the letter key.
//          • CVD status table font size is now an input (cvdTableSizeInput,
//            Tiny/Small/Normal/Large/Huge, default Normal — was hardcoded
//            Small). All six cells use it.
// v20.12 — Three items: RVOL #3 completion, OTE-leg UDT compile fix, and
//          split OB RVOL threshold.
//          • [compile fix] The v20.8/v20.10 OTE impulse-leg state
//            (oteLegTop/Bottom/Time/Voided/Frozen) was declared as bare
//            global vars but mutated inside displayStructure() (a function).
//            Pine v6 forbids reassigning a bare global from a function, so it
//            threw "Cannot modify global variable". Wrapped the state in an
//            `oteLeg` UDT (oteLegState) — field mutation IS allowed in
//            functions (same pattern as validEqHighPool / streakCounter).
//          • [RVOL #1 calibration] Split the OB volume multiple by scale.
//            After v20.9 made OB RVOL sample the impulse-window peak, swing
//            OBs (40-100 bar impulses) nearly always cleared 1.5×, diluting
//            the institutional flag. New rvolOBThresholdSwingInput (default
//            2.5) for swing OBs; rvolOBThresholdInput (default 1.5) now
//            applies to internal OBs only. obIsInst picks by `internal`.
//          • [RVOL #3 completion] details below.
// v20.12-base — RVOL #3 completion. v20.9 added the rvolVolumeAvailable latch to
//          the ratio math and the retail-trap alert, but NOT to the four
//          dimming/hide render paths (OB, Breaker, iFVG, FVG). On a
//          volumeless feed with RVOL ON + Hide-Low-Vol ON, isInstitutional
//          is false for everything (RVOL na), so those four conditions were
//          all true → every block was set to full transparency and
//          disappeared — the exact failure v20.9's changelog claimed #3
//          prevented. The guard was only effective on the alert side. Added
//          `rvolVolumeAvailable and` to all four render conditions so on
//          volumeless symbols the dimming/hide path is bypassed and blocks
//          render normally.
// v20.11 — Daily-TF guard propagated to the four range trackers + Midnight
//          Open (regression-class fix). Sessions got `timeframe.isintraday`
//          in v20.4 but Asian/London/NY ranges, Initial Balance, and
//          Midnight Open did not. On a Daily+ chart their session-window
//          test latches true on every bar, so the range high/low expanded
//          to the chart's all-time extremes and the *Touched alerts read
//          that garbage; Midnight Open captured once and went stale. All
//          five drivers now require timeframe.isintraday, matching Sessions.
//          AVWAP is intentionally NOT guarded — it has no intraday session
//          window; its MSS/Swing anchors work on any TF and its Daily/
//          Weekly anchors reset correctly on higher timeframes.
// v20.10 — Impulse-Leg OTE follow-up (R1) + fib-line label fix:
//          • [R1] The leg's terminal extreme (top for bull, bottom for bear)
//            is no longer frozen at the BOS bar. Price almost always extends
//            past the break before retracing, so v20.8's break-bar freeze
//            gave a truncated leg → too-deep OTE band that price could
//            reverse from before reaching. Now: origin stays fixed at the
//            swing extreme, but the terminal extreme TRACKS the running
//            high/low after the break and FREEZES on the first bar whose
//            close retraces into the band. New oteLegFrozen latch. Keeps
//            v20.8's no-drift property (locks once entered) while capturing
//            the true leg extent. Only affects 'Impulse Leg' OTE mode.
//          • Fib-line binding fix. ote618Line was always assigned the
//            geometric upper level, which on bearish zones is actually the
//            0.786 retracement, so the 0.618/0.786 lines were swapped for
//            shorts. Invisible while both share oteColor, but wrong if the
//            two are styled differently. Now each line is bound to its true
//            retracement price per direction. Pre-existing (not a v20.8
//            regression).
// v20.9 — RVOL audit fixes (#1-#3):
//         • [#1] OB RVOL now samples the IMPULSE window, not the OB candle.
//           The OB origin is by construction the quiet pullback candle before
//           the break — institutional volume lives in the displacement that
//           follows. Pre-v20.9 sampled volumes.get(parsedIndex) (the
//           low-volume side), so OBs rarely flagged institutional while FVGs
//           (sampled on the push bar) frequently did, under the SAME 1.5×
//           threshold. Now numerator = MAX volume across [OB candle … break
//           bar]; denominator = trailing pre-OB average (origin bar now
//           EXCLUDED, fixing audit #4's self-inflation too). OB and FVG
//           "institutional" now mean the same thing. Opt-in (RVOL off by
//           default); expect more OBs to flag institutional than before —
//           re-tune rvolOBThresholdInput if needed.
//         • [#2] Retail-trap alert + RVOL flags no longer conflate
//           "below threshold" with "volume unmeasurable". Pre-v20.9
//           `not isInstitutional` was true whenever RVOL was na (volumeless
//           symbol / warm-up), so 'Low-RVOL Block Broken' fired on blocks
//           whose volume was never measured. Now requires
//           `not na(originRVOL) and not isInstitutional` (a real low reading).
//         • [#3] Volumeless-symbol guard. New rvolVolumeAvailable latch
//           (true once any bar carries real volume). All RVOL ratios and the
//           retail-trap alert are gated on it, so FX cash / volumeless
//           indices don't (a) hide every OB/FVG via Hide-Low-Vol or (b) fire
//           the trap on every mitigation. Combined with #2.
//         • [#4] Folded into #1 — OB denominator now excludes the origin
//           bar (true RVOL baseline). FVG side unchanged (HTF SMA already
//           ends at the push bar; left as-is to avoid an HTF re-request).
//         • [#5] Early-history window truncation — left as-is (cosmetic,
//           affects only the oldest visible OBs near the buffer start).
// v20.8 — OTE audit fixes (#1-#5):
//         • [#4, safe] Fib-order clamp. oteFib1Input / oteFib2Input were
//           independent; setting Fib1 >= Fib2 produced an inverted box and
//           nonsensical zone. The shared helper now uses
//           fShallow = min(fib1,fib2), fDeep = max(...), so upper > lower
//           always.
//         • [#5, safe] Single source of truth. New oteZoneLevels() helper
//           returns [upper, lower, valid, top, bottom, eq]; both
//           drawOTEZone() and the priceInOTE alert consume it. Kills the
//           duplicated fib math that drifted out of sync once before (v15.3).
//         • [#1/#2/#3, opt-in] New "OTE Anchor" input:
//             Dealing Range (default) = legacy behavior; OTE measured off
//               the trailing.top/bottom envelope shared with Premium/Discount
//               — drifts and widens as the trend extends.
//             Impulse Leg (ICT-correct) = at the swing BOS/CHoCH/MSS that
//               sets bias, the originating leg is captured and FROZEN
//               (swing-low→break for bullish, swing-high→break for bearish).
//               Fib levels stay static (a placeable level, not a drifting
//               zone), the box anchors at the leg origin time, and the zone
//               is VOIDED when price closes beyond the leg origin (bullish:
//               below legBottom; bearish: above legTop) instead of stretching
//               to chase price. New var state: oteLegTop/Bottom/Time/Voided,
//               captured in displayStructure (swing branch, independent of
//               useTrailResetInput), void-checked every bar before render.
//         • [#6] OTE swing-bias latency is by design (swing BOS lag) — not
//           changed; documented in prior versions.
// v20.7 — Market-mechanics audit fixes BS-1 through BS-4:
//         • [BS-1] Outside-bar structure blackout fixed. When one bar
//           closes through BOTH the prior swing high and swing low
//           (engulfing / displacement / stop-run-and-reverse), pre-v20.7
//           silenced BOTH the bull and bear cross → no BOS/CHoCH/MSS/OB on
//           the highest-information candles. Now resolved by close location
//           within the bar: close in upper third → bull wins; lower third
//           → bear wins; middle third → silence both (legacy, ambiguous
//           case only).
//         • [BS-2] Multi-level swing-sweep tracking. Pre-v20.7 only the
//           single most-recent swing high and low were watched for sweeps;
//           older untouched swings (the real stop magnets) went unmonitored
//           once superseded. New swingSweepLevelsInput (default 5) keeps the
//           last N unswept swing highs and lows under surveillance via
//           watch-list arrays (reuses the eqPool UDT). A level leaves the
//           list when swept (wick-through + close back) or cleanly broken
//           (close beyond). Set to 1 for legacy single-level behavior.
//         • [BS-3] CVD-divergence magnitude filter is now leg-length
//           normalized. Pre-v20.7 the numerator was the cumulative CVD
//           change across the whole pivot-to-pivot span but the denominator
//           was only the per-bar average |delta|, so the ratio scaled with
//           leg length — wide pivot pairs scored high purely from bar count.
//           Added a lastBarIndex field to the pivot UDT (and populated it in
//           getCurrentStructure + the custom CVD pivot detector) so the
//           denominator now multiplies by bars-between-pivots, yielding a
//           true per-bar divergence intensity.
//         • [BS-4] Displacement + structure-quality now use a fast ATR.
//           Pre-v20.7 both the MSS displacement test and the
//           Weak/Medium/Strong quality score measured a single-bar event
//           against ATR(200) — a slow baseline that stays stale across
//           volatility regimes (post-contraction it's still inflated, so
//           real displacement reads as Weak / MSS won't trigger). New
//           dispQualityATRLenInput (default 14) feeds ONLY displacement +
//           quality; EQ-tolerance and min-penetration keep ATR(200) for
//           stability. Set the input to 200 to restore exact prior behavior.
// v20.6 — OB search cap blind-spot fix (follow-up to v20.4 anchor input):
//         • v20.4 added an OB Search Anchor toggle so users could pick
//           whether the cap clips bars near origin or bars near broken
//           pivot. But whichever half got clipped was a hard blind spot —
//           if the OB candle happened to live in that half, the cluster
//           search returned na and the indicator fell through to the
//           extreme-high/low fallback (which uses a different selection
//           criterion). Different anchor = different blind spot, same
//           problem of equal size.
//         • v20.6 adds an automatic SECONDARY scan. Flow now is:
//             1. Snapshot the full natural window (origin → broken)
//                BEFORE applying the cap.
//             2. Apply the cap → primary window (a subset of natural).
//             3. Scan primary for the latest opposite-color candle. If
//                found, use it (no behavior change for the common case).
//             4. If primary returned na AND the window was capped, scan
//                the OTHER half of the natural window. This catches OBs
//                that landed in the previously-blind half.
//             5. If that's STILL na, fall through to the extreme-high
//                /low fallback — now also extended to cover the full
//                natural window (was only covering the primary half).
//         • Net effect: the OB Search Anchor input becomes a PREFERENCE
//           dial instead of a blind-spot risk. The chosen half wins
//           ties (preferred-half latest-found beats other-half latest-
//           found). The opposite half only gets scanned when the
//           preferred half has nothing. Worst case is now "found the
//           secondary-half OB instead of nothing" — strictly better.
//         • Cost: the secondary scan only runs when primary returned na
//           AND the window was larger than the cap, which is rare. In
//           the common case (window ≤ cap, OR primary finds something)
//           there's zero extra cost.
// v20.5 — Two strategy-logic fixes from quant-design audit:
//         • [OB confluence FVG] Replaces the live fairValueGaps array
//           lookup with a HISTORICAL 3-bar FVG pattern detection on the
//           highs/lows arrays around parsedIndex. Pre-v20.5, when an OB
//           was identified the code asked "is there a CURRENTLY ACTIVE
//           FVG overlapping the OB price range?" — but FVGs that existed
//           when the OB was born and have since been mitigated were no
//           longer in the array, so older OBs were denied their FVG
//           confluence point even though they were structurally strong
//           at birth. New check walks +0/+1/+2 offsets from parsedIndex
//           and checks for a 3-bar FVG (bar1.high < bar3.low or
//           bar1.low > bar3.high) at each — i.e., the canonical FVG
//           formation that the OB or its immediate impulse-start would
//           have produced. Score is now born-on assessment, not
//           current-state grading.
//         • [CVD bias table] Bias row now uses a rolling N-bar sum of
//           cvdBarDelta instead of the sign of cumCVD. cumCVD
//           accumulates from the chart's first loaded bar, so its sign
//           reflects "what did flow look like since the chart loaded" —
//           which is meaningless when the chart loaded mid-rally and
//           the market has been crashing for days. New cvdBiasWindowInput
//           (default 50) controls the rolling window. Bias colour and
//           CVD-row colour now both flow from the rolling-window sign,
//           so they can't disagree with the user's actual recent flow
//           experience. The raw cumulative cumCVD value is still shown
//           in the first row for absolute reference.
// v20.4 — Five fixes: two from OB-cluster-search audit + three from the
//         quant-review follow-up:
//         • [OB] Search cap direction is now user-selectable. New
//           obSearchAnchorInput dropdown:
//             Origin (legacy default) — scan forward from origin pivot up
//               to obSearchCap bars. When the natural origin→broken
//               window exceeds the cap, bars near the broken pivot are
//               trimmed. Matches "first opposite candle near swing
//               low/high" interpretation.
//             Break — scan backward from broken pivot up to obSearchCap
//               bars. Bars near origin pivot are trimmed. Matches "last
//               opposite candle before structural break" interpretation.
//           Only matters when the natural window is larger than the cap;
//           otherwise behavior is unchanged.
//         • [OB] Dead-code cleanup in storeOrderBlock(). Removed unused
//           `int _opensSize = opens.size()` local and the redundant
//           `if i >= 0 and i < _closesSize` inner guard inside both
//           cluster loops (searchStart and searchEnd are already clamped
//           to valid array indices before the loops execute).
//         • [Sessions] Daily+ timeframe guard. On daily/weekly/monthly
//           bars, every intraday session window fits entirely inside the
//           bar's 24h+ duration → tracker.active latched true forever →
//           one oversized session box stretched across the chart. Sessions
//           are inherently intraday concepts; suppressed entirely outside
//           `timeframe.isintraday`.
//         • [Structure quality] Warm-up na guard on the ATR denominator.
//           For the first ~14 bars, ta.atr(200) and ta.atr(14) both
//           return na, propagating through math.max() and making
//           _bullDisp / _bearDisp = na. The Weak/Medium/Strong ternary
//           then fell through to 'Weak' for every internal break in
//           warm-up. Wrapped the denom in nz(atrMeasure, syminfo.mintick)
//           so the displacement ratio is finite from bar 1.
//         • [Skipped] Midnight Open 1-minute window fragility. Real edge
//           case (illiquid instruments missing the 00:00 NY bar), but the
//           proposed dayofweek-change fallback has its own failure mode
//           on Sunday session reopens (would latch Sun-evening open as
//           "midnight"). Deferred to a future version pending a proper
//           two-tier latch design.
// v20.3 — Per-session local timezone anchoring (BEHAVIOR CHANGE on session boxes):
//         • New "Session Anchor Mode" input with two choices:
//             Per-Session Local (new default) — each of the four sessions
//               evaluates in its OWN market timezone using local business
//               hours. London tracks UK BST/GMT, Sydney tracks Australian
//               AEST/AEDT (opposite hemisphere DST), Tokyo has no DST, NY
//               tracks US EST/EDT. All four boundaries remain correct
//               year-round even when the four regions' DST schedules
//               disagree.
//             Single Timezone (ICT) — legacy behavior. All sessions in
//               one timezone (default America/New_York) with NY-clock
//               hours. Use this for classic ICT methodology where
//               everything is referenced in NY time.
//         • Per-session hardcoded mappings:
//             Sydney   → Australia/Sydney  07:00-16:00 local
//             Tokyo    → Asia/Tokyo        09:00-18:00 local
//             London   → Europe/London     08:00-17:00 local
//             New York → America/New_York  08:00-17:00 local
//         • The existing "Session Timezone" input is renamed to "Session
//           Timezone (Single mode)" and is now consulted ONLY when Anchor
//           Mode = Single. Also added Asia/Dubai to its dropdown.
//         • Kill Zones and Silver Bullet windows are NOT affected — those
//           remain anchored to kzTimezoneInput (default NY) because the
//           ICT kill-zone concepts are inherently NY-time-defined.
//         • inSessionWindow() function signature changed to accept an
//           explicit timezone parameter, replacing the previous implicit
//           sessTimezoneInput closure.
// v20.2 — Session-box history window control:
//         • Two new inputs in the Sessions group:
//             sessHistoryModeInput  — 'All History' (default; legacy) or
//                                     'Custom (Last N Days)'.
//             sessHistoryDaysInput  — N, range 1-60, default 5.
//         • In Custom mode, session boxes only render for sessions
//           starting within N days of the latest loaded bar.
//             N=1  → today only.
//             N=5  → trading week.
//             N=21 → roughly a calendar month.
//         • Implementation: state tracking inside updateSession()
//           (tracker.active, .prevActive, .sessionHigh, .sessionLow)
//           still updates every bar so window-boundary transitions don't
//           fire spurious "new session" events. Only the box/label
//           CREATION block is gated by the new drawAllowed parameter.
//           If a session started before the window opens, no box is
//           created and the expand block's `if not na(tracker.sessionBox)`
//           guard silently no-ops the geometry updates.
//         • Default is 'All History' so existing users see no change.
// v20.1 — Audit follow-up on v20.0:
//         • [HIGH] Structure-quality filter no longer leaks state through
//           filtered events. Pre-v20.1 the alert assignments / label draws
//           / OB storage were gated by _bullPasses (and _bearPasses), but
//           the snap-pivot `crossed` flag, `t_rend.bias` flip, and
//           trail-reset block all ran UNCONDITIONALLY on the validBull/
//           BearCross path. A "Weak BOS" filtered out of alerts would
//           still flip the trend bias and consume the pivot — so
//           subsequent CHoCH/MSS detections evaluated against a corrupted
//           bias state and downstream signals were silently wrong on the
//           trades that did fire. Wrapped all state mutations inside the
//           _bullPasses / _bearPasses gate so the filter is now atomic.
//         • [MEDIUM] OB confluence Premium/Discount check is now
//           bias-aware. Pre-v20.1 a bearish OB sitting in discount or a
//           bullish OB sitting in premium got +1 confluence — both are
//           directionally-wrong setups per ICT. Now only a bullish OB in
//           discount or a bearish OB in premium scores the P/D point.
//         • [MINOR] obConfluenceMinScoreInput tooltip now spells out the
//           three feeder dependencies (RVOL, FVG tracking, P/D trailing
//           extremes ready) so users understand why score=3 may be
//           unreachable in some configurations.
//         • [MINOR] MSS bypass comment in the structure-quality block
//           rewritten honestly. Pre-v20.1 the comment claimed MSS is
//           "already strength-validated" and so doesn't need a second
//           filter. Accurate only when mssATRMultInput / mssBodyRatioInput
//           are tuned at-or-above the Strong thresholds (1.0 ATR / 0.6
//           body ratio). New comment explains the two filter chains
//           are independent and how to align them if the user wants a
//           single unified strength cap.
// v20.0 — Feature release. Five new capabilities, all off-by-default:
//         1. EQ tolerance ticks floor. New equalHighsLowsTicksInput (default 0)
//            adds an absolute lower bound on the EQH/EQL tolerance, so the
//            effective threshold is max(ATR_factor × ATR, ticks × mintick).
//            Fixes the JPY/index-futures problem where 0.1×ATR was too loose.
//            Default 0 = legacy ATR-only behavior.
//         2. Low-RVOL FVG/OB break alert. New lowRvolBreakAlertInput toggle +
//            'Low-RVOL Block Broken' alertcondition. Fires when a
//            non-institutional FVG or OB (RVOL below threshold at formation)
//            gets mitigated — ICT "retail trap" signal. Combined into one
//            alert slot to preserve output budget.
//         3. Session-aware OB tagging. New sessionOrigin field on the
//            orderBlock UDT, populated at creation by classifying the OB
//            candle's hour-of-day in NY time into Asian / London / NY / Off.
//            Optional visual badge (A/L/NY) via showOBSessionTagInput.
//            Optional filter (obSessionFilterInput) — when set to a specific
//            session, OBs from other sessions render fully transparent.
//            Breaker conversion preserves the parent OB's sessionOrigin.
//         4. Structure quality filter. New structureMinQualityInput
//            (All / Medium+ / Strong Only). Computes a Weak/Medium/Strong
//            score for every BOS/CHoCH from (a) displacement of close past
//            the broken level in ATRs and (b) body-to-range ratio. Gates the
//            alert, the structure label, and OB storage so weak BOS bars
//            don't pollute the chart or the OB stream. MSS always passes
//            (it's already a strength-validated CHoCH path). Optional badge
//            (S/M/W) appended to structure labels via
//            showStructureQualityBadgeInput.
//         5. OB confluence scoring. New confluenceScore field on the
//            orderBlock UDT (0-3), populated at creation: +1 for
//            isInstitutional, +1 for FVG-range overlap, +1 for
//            Premium/Discount zone membership of the OB midpoint. Optional
//            ★N badge via showOBConfluenceScoreInput. New
//            'High Confluence OB Formed' alertcondition fires when the
//            score meets the user-set obConfluenceMinScoreInput threshold.
//            Breaker conversion preserves the parent OB's score.
//
//         Output-budget summary: +2 alertconditions (Low-RVOL Block Broken,
//         High Confluence OB Formed). All other features are pure data /
//         UDT field additions with zero output cost. Total still under the
//         64-output ceiling.
// v19.10 — Silver Bullet visually separated from Kill Zones:
//          • Bottom ribbon was a single plotshape with squares for both
//            KZ and SB, so when an SB window overlapped a KZ window (SB
//            AM ⊂ London Close KZ, SB LDN ⊂ London Open KZ, etc.) the
//            two markers were indistinguishable. Split into two plotshapes
//            at the same location.bottom — KZ uses shape.square, SB uses
//            shape.diamond. When both fire on the same bar, the diamond
//            overlays the square so user sees "this is a KZ AND a Silver
//            Bullet sub-window". Cost: +2 outputs (was 2, now 4); still
//            far under the 64 ceiling.
// v19.9 — Five follow-up audit fixes (quality-of-life pass):
//         • Initial Balance age expiry. New ibMaxAgeHoursInput (default
//           23h) mirrors NDOG's auto-expire. After the IB session ends
//           the lines/labels now fade (color set to na) once they're
//           older than the configured age. Was previously persisting
//           for ~21-23 hours after each IB completed, cluttering the
//           chart with stale levels until the next IB reset overwrote
//           them. Setting 0 restores the legacy "never expire" behavior.
//         • CVD divergence magnitude filter. New cvdDivMinMagnitudeInput
//           (default 0 = off, legacy). When > 0, requires the
//           pivot-to-pivot CVD delta to be at least N× the recent
//           SMA(|cvdBarDelta|, 50) before firing the divergence alert/
//           label. Normalized so the threshold is timeframe-agnostic.
//           Removes the chop-divergence noise floor that the original
//           sign-only check produced.
//         • EQ pool eviction by lowest streak (was: oldest dies).
//           updateEqPools() now scans index 1..n on overflow and drops
//           the pool with the fewest touches, breaking ties by keeping
//           older entries. Newly added pool (index 0) is always kept
//           — gives fresh price levels a chance to accumulate touches
//           before competing for the cap. Matches ICT's preference for
//           high-conviction (many-touch) liquidity pools.
//         • OB search multiplier exposed as input. New
//           obSearchCapMultiplierInput (default 5, range 2-15) controls
//           the swing-OB back-scan window. Internal OB scan kept at
//           fixed 3× to bound per-bar cost. Useful for H4+ timeframes
//           or long consolidations where the real OB candle can be
//           older than the previous 100-bar cap.
//         • EQ label drawing + alerts gated on barstate.isconfirmed.
//           Pool tracking (updateEqPools, streak counter) still updates
//           every tick so internal state stays current; only the
//           visible EQH/EQL labels and the equalHighs/equalLows alerts
//           are confirmed-only, preventing duplicate labels piling up
//           during a high-tick forming bar.
// v19.8 — UX polish:
//         • Kill Zones + Silver Bullet windows moved from full-height
//           bgcolor() washes to a thin bottom ribbon via plotshape() at
//           location=location.bottom. Same information, no more color
//           overlay washing across the candles.
//           Implementation note: the first attempt split into 6 separate
//           plotshape calls and blew the 64-output ceiling (RE10140).
//           bgcolor() with a series color counts as 1 output, but
//           plotshape() with a series color counts as 2 (Pine treats
//           color= as a second series). 6 × 2 = 12 outputs vs the
//           original 6 × 1 = 6. To stay under the ceiling AND save
//           slots, all KZs + SBs are merged into ONE plotshape with the
//           color chosen by ternary (kill zones never overlap each
//           other in time anyway). Net cost: 2 outputs (down from 6).
//         • Indicator legend / status line de-noised. All 201 input
//           declarations now carry `display = display.none`, so the
//           "Historical Colored Body All All tiny 5 …" stream of input
//           values no longer renders as a long string next to the
//           indicator name. Inputs remain fully accessible via the
//           Settings dialog and the Data Window panel; only the
//           always-visible status-line clutter is suppressed.
// v19.7 — Dead-code cleanup follow-up to v19.6:
//         • parsedHighs / parsedLows arrays removed. After v19.6 dropped
//           the high-volatility-bar swap, the parsed* arrays held values
//           identical to highs / lows but were still pushed every bar
//           (two 5,000-entry float buffers of duplicate data). The
//           OB-fallback max/min scan now slices highs / lows directly.
//           Cosmetic — saves memory but no behavior change.
//         • Skipped the audit's second follow-up (EQ-pool sweep order =
//           oldest-first). The reverse iteration is the safe pattern for
//           array.remove() during the loop, and same-bar multi-pool
//           sweeps produce identical visible output regardless of order.
// v19.6 — Six audit fixes (quant-review pass):
//         • OB cluster search dropped its `consNon > 2` early break. Loop
//           iterates oldest→newest with lastFound overwriting on every
//           opposite-color hit; the break short-circuited to the FIRST
//           opposite-color candle instead of the LATEST, misplacing OB
//           origins on wide consolidations / extended CHoCH legs. Scan
//           now runs the full searchEnd; window is already capped at
//           5× swingsLengthInput (~100 bars) so cost is bounded.
//         • FVG / iFVG / VI mitigation gained the same minPen guard
//           OBs/BBs already use (ATR-fraction + mintick floor). A 1-tick
//           body close past the gap edge no longer kills the gap; price
//           must penetrate by at least minPen. Symmetric with the rest
//           of the indicator and filters micro-wick noise in low-ATR
//           regimes.
//         • Multi-pool EQH/EQL tracking replaces the single
//           validEqHighPool / validEqLowPool. New `eqPool` UDT, arrays
//           of pools (cap MAX_EQ_POOLS = 5), and a new updateEqPools()
//           helper. Each pool's level/wick/anchorBarIdx is locked at
//           creation; only streak and lastTouchBarIdx update on
//           subsequent in-tolerance matches. Fixes (a) the audit's
//           "pool drifts to freshest pivot" finding — ICT treats the
//           original untouched pool as the magnet — and (b) the
//           single-pool-per-side limitation — multiple distinct EQH/EQL
//           clusters at different prices now coexist and are each
//           sweep-monitored independently. Sweep detection iterates the
//           array; pools are removed on sweep (with alert) or clean
//           break-through (no alert).
//         • useTrailResetInput default flipped from false to true. The
//           old default ratcheted trailing extremes monotonically
//           between swing pivots, inflating the Premium/Discount/OTE
//           box on ranging days and divorcing the zone from current
//           structure. ICT convention is to track the most recent leg,
//           so ON is the more sensible default. Toggle OFF to restore
//           the legacy wide-envelope behavior.
//         • parsedHigh / parsedLow no longer swap on wide-range bars.
//           Previously `highVolatilityBar ? low : high` excluded
//           displacement candles from the OB-fallback max/min search —
//           but ICT considers wide-range bars STRONG OB candidates
//           (high-conviction reversal). Now wide bars contribute their
//           actual high/low and are eligible as fallback OB origins.
//           The volatilityMeasure / highVolatilityBar flag remains for
//           downstream consumers that still want the filter.
// v19.5 — Two NDOG/NWOG visibility fixes (regressions from v19.3 / v19.4):
//         • NDOG/NWOG hybrid fill check. v19.4 removed the v16.8 same-bar
//           skip outright, which made gaps invisible on FX timeframes ≥
//           ~5m: the rollover bar's range almost always covers gap.bottom
//           (bullish) or gap.top (bearish), so the bias-aware check fired
//           on the SAME execution as createOpeningGap() and the box was
//           deleted before the user could see it. Restored the skip so
//           the gap renders for at least one bar, but added a one-bar
//           RETROACTIVE fill check (`time[1] == gap.startTime` reading
//           low[1]/high[1]) so the audit's "stale unfilled gaps" concern
//           is still addressed — fills are now caught on bar+1 instead of
//           silently missed. From bar+2 onward, normal current-bar
//           checking runs.
//         • ICT NY NWOG anchor was non-functional on FX feeds. v19.3
//           detected "Friday 17:00 ET" via
//           `time(timeframe.period, '1700-1701:6', 'America/New_York')`,
//           which requires a bar OPENING at 17:00 NY Friday. FX brokers
//           close the Friday session at 17:00 NY, so the last Friday bar
//           CLOSES at 17:00 but doesn't open there → atFri17ET never
//           fired → nwogICTPrevClose stayed na → no NWOG was ever
//           created in ICT NY mode on any FX symbol. Rewrote the
//           detection: track whether each bar is inside the NY-anchored
//           week via dayofweek/hour, latch close while inside, and
//           detect the Sun 17:00 NY transition either via an
//           inICTWeek[1]==false flip OR a > 6-hour gap between
//           consecutive bars (so brokers that skip weekend bars also
//           trigger correctly).
// v19.4 — Two follow-up audit fixes:
//         • NDOG/NWOG opening-bar fill detection. The v16.8 `if time ==
//           gap.startTime: continue` skip in updateAndMitigateGaps() was
//           defensive against the old strict-span and close-traversal fill
//           logic. v19.3 replaced both, making the skip overly broad: it
//           suppressed genuine same-bar fills (price retracing to gap.bottom
//           on a bullish opening candle, or gap.top on a bearish one),
//           leaving stale "unfilled" gap markers on chart indefinitely.
//           Removed the skip; the bias-aware check correctly handles the
//           same-bar fill case.
//         • OTE / Strong-Weak H-L / Premium-Discount one-bar lag fix.
//           The render block was running BEFORE getCurrentStructure() and
//           displayStructure() inside the main execution section, so OTE
//           direction and Strong/Weak labels read swingTrend.bias from the
//           PREVIOUS bar. On a BOS/CHoCH bar that flipped the bias, visuals
//           lagged one bar before catching up. Moved the entire render
//           block (updateTrailingExtremes + drawHighLowSwings +
//           drawPremiumDiscountZones + drawOTEZone) to AFTER both
//           displayStructure() calls so it sees the current bar's bias.
// v19.3 — NDOG/NWOG audit fixes:
//         • NDOG/NWOG fill detection is now bias-aware. Previous condition
//           `high >= gap.top and low <= gap.bottom` required a single bar
//           to span the ENTIRE gap top-to-bottom, so on intraday timeframes
//           most genuine fills went undetected and stale gaps cluttered the
//           chart indefinitely. Replaced with the ICT-standard check: a
//           bullish opening gap fills when `low <= gap.bottom` (price
//           returns down to the prev-close level); a bearish opening gap
//           fills when `high >= gap.top`. `gap.bias` was already stored at
//           creation, just never consulted. The redundant close-traversal
//           fallback is removed — fully subsumed by the new bias-aware check.
//         • createOpeningGap() threshold loosened from `>` to `>=` so a
//           clean 1-tick opening gap is registered as a gap. The intent of
//           the threshold is to skip the equal-open=equal-close no-gap case;
//           1-tick separation IS a gap by definition. Same `>=` applied to
//           the NDOG/NWOG alertcondition for consistency.
//         • New "NWOG Anchor" input. Default "TV Weekly" preserves legacy
//           behavior (TradingView's weekly bar boundary, FX-aligned). New
//           "ICT NY (Fri/Sun 17:00 ET)" mode anchors strictly to the
//           classic ICT NWOG window — useful on crypto/futures/equities
//           where TV's weekly bar doesn't align with the NY-session week.
//           Requires intraday data with bars at Sun 17:00 ET; won't work
//           on RTH-only equity feeds.
// v19.2 — Audit-driven bug-fix release + Initial Balance feature:
//         • EQH/EQL sweep detector now references a separate validated-EQ-pool
//           level (validEqHigh/LowPool, wrapped in the existing pivot UDT for
//           in-function field mutation). The previous code latched against
//           equalHigh/Low.currentLevel, which is overwritten on every length-3
//           pivot, so "EQH/EQL Sweep" alerts fired on any plain swing high/low
//           wick rather than only on validated EQ pools.
//         • HTF FVG request.security offsets shifted by -1 across the tuple
//           ([close[2]/open[2]/high[3]/low[3] → close[1]/open[1]/high[2]/low[2],
//           recent at no-offset). Under lookahead_off, the previous indices
//           skipped the most-recently-finalized HTF bar entirely, detecting
//           each FVG one full HTF bar after it could have been confirmed.
//         • OB volatility filter's non-ATR branch was ta.cum(ta.tr)/bar_index,
//           a chart-history-dependent running mean. Replaced with a 500-bar
//           rolling SMA of TR (deterministic across history reloads).
//         • FVG auto-threshold replaced its cumulative running mean with a
//           100-HTF-bar rolling history of |barDeltaPercent|, updated only on
//           newTimeframe transitions. Also fixes a latent miscalibration where
//           the previous denominator was chart-bar count while the numerator
//           only accumulated on HTF-bar boundaries — on a 1m chart watching
//           4H FVGs the threshold was ~1/240 of intent.
//         • Internal-break confluence filter no longer fails closed during
//           warm-up. The level-distinctness check (snapInternalHigh vs
//           snapSwingHigh) propagated na before the first swing pivot formed,
//           silencing every internal break in that window when the
//           internalFilterConfluenceInput toggle was on. Now falls back to the
//           bullishBar/bearishBar candle-character check alone when the swing
//           snap level isn't ready yet.
//         • drawLevels() same-timeframe branch now reads high[1]/low[1]/time[1]
//           instead of current-bar high/low/time, so on a daily chart with
//           Daily Levels enabled the "PDH" line plots yesterday's high (as
//           labeled) instead of today's in-progress high. Same fix applies to
//           weekly and monthly levels viewed on their native timeframe.
//         • PWH/PWL line left-anchor now uses a new currentWeekStartTime
//           request.security value instead of currentDayStartTime, so the
//           weekly-level lines start at the current week's open rather than
//           today's open. drawPDLevel() gained an optional leftAnchor
//           parameter to support both call sites; existing PD/MO callers
//           keep the daily anchor.
//         • Initial Balance feature: new "Initial Balance" input group with
//           configurable session (default 0930-1030 ET, market-profile RTH
//           first hour), optional midline and 1× range extensions. Lines and
//           labels render the same way the Asian/London/NY ranges do. No
//           alertcondition added — the script is at the 64-output ceiling
//           that v16.6 and v18.4 were already managing.
//         • Indicator title + on-chart name bumped to v19.2 to match.
// v19.1 — Fixes from external analysis pass:
//         • bullishBar / bearishBar inverted in displayStructure (confluence
//           filter). The flags `bullishBar := upperWick >= lowerWick` and
//           `bearishBar := lowerWick >= upperWick` were the OPPOSITE of
//           ICT/SMC convention — a large lower wick is buying pressure
//           (bullish-character bar), a large upper wick is selling
//           rejection (bearish-character). Swapped the assignments so the
//           confluence filter accepts the right kind of confirming candle.
//           Effective only when internalFilterConfluenceInput = ON (was
//           OFF by default, so most users were never affected).
//         • Swing OB search cap bumped from 3x to 5x of Swing Length
//           (60 → 100 bars at default Swing Length = 20). Fixes occasional
//           wrong-origin-candle landings on long consolidations or wide
//           CHoCH where the actual OB candle is older than the previous
//           60-bar limit. Internal OB cap unchanged at 3x.
//         • AVWAP tooltip now notes that symbols without volume data
//           (some indices) won't render an AVWAP line.
// v19.0 — Rename EQH/EQL pivot-length input for discoverability:
//         • Renamed input label "Bars Confirmation" → "EQH/EQL Pivot Length"
//           and expanded tooltip. No behavior change; the input
//           equalHighsLowsLengthInput has always controlled the pivot
//           lookback for EQH/EQL detection, independently from swing
//           (Swing Length) and internal (Internal Swing Length) lookbacks.
//           The legacy name was inherited from the original LuxAlgo code.
//         • Also added a maxval cap (50) for the slider UI; previously
//           unbounded.
//         • No new outputs. Volume Profile and SMT divergence will live in
//           companion indicators rather than bloat this one further.
// v18.9 — Independent EQH/EQL pivot source override:
//         • New input "EQH/EQL Pivot Source" in EQ group. Options:
//             Follow Main — inherit global pivotSourceInput (default)
//             Body        — match body extremes (filters wick noise)
//             Wick        — match actual high/low (authentic ICT
//                           liquidity pool detection — where stops sit)
//         • Affects only the EQ-comparison level, not pivot detection
//           itself. Pivot detection still uses the global Pivot Source
//           via the existing bodyHigh/bodyLow series. This is intentional:
//           leg() detection at one source + level comparison at another
//           gives a sensible hybrid without a full pivot-stream refactor.
// v18.8 — CVD custom pivot length + EQH/EQL freshness timeout:
//         • CVD divergence detection now supports three pivot sources:
//             Swing    — existing swing pivots (Swing Length, default 20)
//             Internal — existing internal pivots (Internal Length, def 5)
//             Custom   — new dedicated CVD pivots at user-set length
//                        (default 10, range 3-50)
//           Resolves the user's request for a CVD lookback independent
//           from both swing structure and internal structure. The toggle
//           input (cvdUseInternalPivotsInput, bool) is replaced by a
//           dropdown (cvdPivotSourceInput, string). Existing saved
//           settings will reset to default "Swing"; users on Internal
//           need to re-select.
//         • EQH/EQL freshness timeout. New optional input
//           "EQH/EQL Max Bars Between Matches". When > 0, an EQ match
//           older than N bars resets the streak count back to 1 (the
//           label still draws). Defaults to 0 (disabled) to preserve
//           existing cumulative-streak behavior. Use this to suppress
//           inflated EQH×N badges where matches span large time gaps.
// v18.7 — Fix AVWAP plot 1-bar lag:
//         • The plot() statement for the MSS AVWAP was positioned above
//           the assignment block that computes mssAvwapValue / sets
//           mssAvwapResetThisBar. Because mssAvwapValue is a `var`,
//           plot() at that position captured the PREVIOUS BAR'S final
//           value, producing a visible 1-bar lag (and the linebr "gap"
//           appearing on the bar AFTER the actual MSS reset). Moved the
//           plot() to after the AVWAP computation block so the current
//           bar's freshly-computed value reaches the chart on its own bar.
// v18.6 — Decouple CVD divergence lookback from swing-structure lookback:
//         • New input "CVD Use Internal Pivots". When ON, CVD divergence
//           triggers off the internal pivot stream (Internal Swing Length,
//           default 5) instead of the swing pivot stream (Swing Length,
//           default 20). Use case: keep swing structure quality at 20 bars
//           while getting faster divergence confirmation at 5 bars.
//         • Implemented by snapshotting cumCVD on internal pivots too
//           (previously only swing pivots got CVD snapshots).
//         • No new alerts. Single existing alertcondition fires regardless
//           of which pivot stream produced the divergence.
// v18.5 — AVWAP MSS scope option:
//         • Split the AVWAP anchor-type dropdown's 'MSS' option into two:
//             'MSS'       — reset on any confirmed MSS (internal + swing)
//             'MSS Swing' — reset on confirmed swing MSS only
//           Lets users choose between frequent resets (more responsive but
//           noisy) and rarer resets (cleaner trend reference).
// v18.4 — Plot-budget rebalance + AVWAP anchor types + RVOL bug fixes:
//         • Re-combined NDOG+NWOG → "Opening Gap Formed" and NY High+Low
//           → "NY Range Touched" (each saves one output). RE10140 was
//           firing again at 66/64; these revert two of v18.2's restores
//           to bring us back to budget.
//         • AVWAP now has an anchor-type dropdown:
//             - MSS (current behaviour: reset on internal/swing MSS event)
//             - Swing (reset on every new swing high or low pivot)
//             - Daily (reset on new trading day)
//             - Weekly (reset on new trading week)
//           Single plot, user-selected source. No additional plot cost.
//         • FVG RVOL stamping bug fix. v18.0 read volume[2] from the
//           chart timeframe even when fairValueGapsTimeframeInput pointed
//           at a higher timeframe. Now requested via request.security
//           alongside the FVG OHLC tuple so volume aligns to the HTF.
//         • iFVG visual RVOL filter bug fix. iFVGs inherited the parent
//           FVG's RVOL stamp but never applied dimming on render. Now
//           ifvgColor is dimmed (or hidden) the same way FVGs are.
//         • needHistoryArrays cleanup. v18.0 added rvolEnableInput to the
//           gate predicate, causing the 8 ring buffers to accumulate even
//           when only FVG RVOL was needed (which uses request.security,
//           not the arrays). The volumes array is only read by OB RVOL,
//           which is already gated by OB-tracking inputs, so dropping
//           rvolEnableInput from the gate has no functional impact.
// v18.3 — Restore per-zone Kill Zone alerts:
//         • v17.1 collapsed 4 Kill Zone Start alerts (Asian / London Open /
//           NY Open / London Close) into one combined alert to stay under
//           the 64-output cap. With v18.1/v18.2 freeing budget we now have
//           headroom to restore the per-zone alerts.
//         • Silver Bullet alerts (3 windows) remain combined — restoring
//           them would push us to 64/64 (right at the cap with no
//           breathing room). Easy to split if user wants.
//         • Output budget after restore: 62 / 64.
// v18.2 — Restore per-side range / PD / opening-gap alerts:
//         • v17.2 had combined PDH+PDL, NDOG+NWOG, Asian H+L, London H+L,
//           and NY H+L into 5 single alerts to free output-budget for
//           v18's institutional features. With v18.1 dropping PO3 we now
//           have headroom (54 / 64) to restore the 10 per-side alerts.
//         • Re-split into:
//             PDH Touched, PDL Touched (2)
//             NDOG Formed, NWOG Formed (2)
//             Asian High Touched, Asian Low Touched (2)
//             London High Touched, London Low Touched (2)
//             NY High Touched, NY Low Touched (2)
//         • Output budget after restore: 59 / 64 (5 slots still free).
// v18.1 — Removed Power of 3 (PO3) module:
//         • Dropped the entire PO3 phase classifier (inputs, state vars,
//           detection block, status label, alertcondition). User feedback
//           was that the static phase label cluttered the chart and the
//           session-window classification was too rigid for non-FX
//           instruments. The freed output slot returns to the budget.
//         • Net: 1 input group removed, 1 alertcondition removed, ~40
//           lines of code removed. No effect on any other feature.
// v18.0 — Institutional-footprint feature pack:
//         • Volume-validated OB / FVG ("RVOL stamping"). At creation,
//           computes RVOL = volume / SMA(volume, N) of the originating
//           bar. OBs/FVGs above the threshold are flagged isInstitutional
//           and rendered at full opacity; non-institutional structures
//           are rendered dimmed (or hidden entirely via a per-feature
//           "show only high-volume" toggle). No new alerts — opt-in
//           visual filter.
//         • Volume Imbalance (VI). ICT-distinct from FVG: a body-to-body
//           gap between consecutive bars (max(open,close)[1] strictly
//           below min(open,close) for bullish; symmetric for bearish).
//           Drawn as small boxes; mitigated when body crosses far edge.
//           One combined alert "Volume Imbalance Formed".
//         • Anchored VWAP from latest MSS (Market Structure Shift).
//           Resets cumulative PV / volume on every confirmed MSS event;
//           plotted as a continuous line on the price chart. One alert
//           "Price Tagged MSS AVWAP" when price wicks the level.
//         • Liquidity Pool clustering. Equal-Highs / Equal-Lows now
//           track a streak counter (`EQH×N` / `EQL×N` badges) so a 3rd
//           or 4th consecutive equal touch is visible at a glance —
//           higher-conviction sweep target.
//         • Power of 3 (PO3) day cycle [REMOVED in v18.1].
// v17.2 — Alert-budget cleanup ahead of v18 feature additions:
//         • Removed 4 legacy *OB Breakout (mitigation) alerts. The same
//           event is captured by the corresponding *Breaker Formed alert
//           when Breaker tracking is enabled, and the *OB Formed alerts
//           cover the formation side. Net: −4 outputs.
//         • Combined PDH + PDL touch alerts into a single
//           "PD Level Touched". Net: −1 output.
//         • Combined NDOG Formed + NWOG Formed into "Opening Gap Formed".
//           Net: −1 output.
//         • Combined Asian/London/NY High+Low range-touch alerts into
//           three single "<Session> Range Touched" alerts. Net: −3 outputs.
//         Total budget freed: 9 outputs. Sets up v18 institutional-
//         footprint additions (RVOL/VI/AVWAP/LP/PO3) without re-hitting
//         RE10140.
// v17.1 — Plot-budget fix:
//         • TradingView caps regular indicators at 64 outputs (plots +
//           alertconditions + bgcolor calls). v17.0 added 4 new alerts
//           (EQH/EQL sweep + 2× CVD divergence) and tipped the script
//           to 68, triggering RE10140 at runtime.
//         • Collapsed the 4 per-zone Kill Zone Start alerts into a single
//           "Kill Zone Start" alert and the 3 per-window Silver Bullet
//           alerts into a single "Silver Bullet Start" alert (saves 5
//           outputs). Per-zone differentiation was already conveyed by
//           the bgcolor visualisation; the alert title is the only thing
//           that loses granularity. Existing user alerts on the old
//           per-zone titles will need to be re-pointed at the combined
//           alert.
// v17.0 — Bug-fix + feature release:
//         • EQH/EQL sweep detection. Sweeps now fire `Bearish EQH Sweep` /
//           `Bullish EQL Sweep` alerts when price wicks through an Equal
//           High/Low cluster and reverses. Previously only swing pivots
//           generated sweep alerts despite EQH/EQL being explicit ICT
//           liquidity pools.
//         • useTrailResetInput now honours pivotSourceInput on swing-flip
//           reset. Was hardcoded to math.max/min(open, close); in Wick mode
//           this caused a one-cycle desync where Strong/Weak H/L drifted
//           toward the body until updateTrailingExtremes overwrote it.
//         • MSS displacement-offset field split: internalBullish/Bearish
//           and swingBullish/Bearish offsets stored separately. Previously
//           shared a single int → on the rare bar where both internal and
//           swing MSS fired with different offsets, last write won and only
//           one diamond marker rendered. drawDisplacementMarker() helper
//           now dedupes when offsets match.
//         • CVD (Cumulative Volume Delta) — new institutional-footprint
//           module. Per-bar delta = volume * (2·close − high − low) / range
//           (close-position weighted); cumulated chart-wide. Detects CVD
//           divergence at confirmed swing pivots: HH in price + LH in CVD
//           = bearish (distribution); LL in price + HL in CVD = bullish
//           (accumulation). Markers placed at the pivot bar; alertconditions
//           emitted; optional top-right status table shows live CVD value.
//           Works on any instrument with `volume` (most equities/futures/
//           crypto); silently zero on volume-less symbols (some indices).
// v16.9 — Code-quality cleanup release:
//         • Replaced the 10-branch hardcoded `low[N]` / `high[N]` ladder for
//           MSS displacement label placement with native Pine v6 dynamic
//           series indexing (`low[displacementBullOffset]`). The ladder
//           silently capped any offset > 8 to N=9; harmless under the
//           current maxval=10 input cap, but a future-bump foot-gun.
//         • pushBounded() history-array writes now gated behind a single
//           `needHistoryArrays` flag (OB tracking OR MTF level drawing).
//           When all consumers are off, the eight 5000-entry float/int
//           ring buffers no longer accumulate per bar.
// v16.8 — Follow-up bug-fix release:
//         • New "OB Formed" alerts (Internal/Swing × Bullish/Bearish). The
//           legacy *OrderBlock alerts only fired on mitigation despite their
//           "Breakout" naming, leaving no way to alert on OB creation. The
//           legacy alerts are unchanged for backward compat; their messages
//           now say "mitigated" instead of "broke" for clarity.
//         • NDOG / NWOG no longer evaluated for fill on the same bar they
//           are created. The legacy close[1]-vs-gap.bottom traversal check
//           referenced close[1] from BEFORE the gap existed, occasionally
//           killing newly-formed gaps instantly on the rollover bar.
//         • Internal Order Block border colour now matches Breaker Block
//           behaviour (visible border) instead of being na, fixing a
//           cosmetic asymmetry where internal OBs looked "borderless" while
//           internal BBs always rendered with a border.
// v16.7 — Bug-fix release:
//         • Liquidity sweep now uses actual wick high/low of the swing pivot
//           bar instead of the body-source level. Fixes phantom sweeps when
//           Pivot Source = Body (any wick over the body was incorrectly
//           registering as a sweep).
//         • PDH/PDL/Midnight Open touch alerts no longer misfire on day
//           rollover. Edge-detection now requires the level itself to be
//           unchanged from the previous bar (filters spurious triggers when
//           pdHigh/midnightOpenPrice jumps to a new value).
//         • iFVG box construction normalised with math.max/min so the two
//           halves render in a deterministic top/bottom order regardless of
//           which parent FVG bias produced them.
//         • Auto-disables Kill Zones, Session Boxes, and Silver Bullet windows
//           on equity instruments (stock, fund, dr, ietf) since session-based
//           ICT timing is designed for FX/futures/crypto, not stocks.

//@version=6
indicator('Smart Money Concepts [v20.16]', 'SMC v20.16', overlay = true, max_labels_count = 500, max_lines_count = 500, max_boxes_count = 500)

//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Constants
//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
BULLISH_LEG  = 1
BEARISH_LEG  = 0
BULLISH      = +1
BEARISH      = -1
GREEN        = #089981
RED          = #F23645
BLUE         = #2157f3
GRAY         = #878b94
MONO_BULLISH = #b2b5be
MONO_BEARISH = #5d606b
HISTORICAL   = 'Historical'
PRESENT      = 'Present'
COLORED      = 'Colored'
MONOCHROME   = 'Monochrome'
ALL          = 'All'
BOS          = 'BOS'
CHOCH        = 'CHoCH'
MSS          = 'MSS'
TINY         = size.tiny
SMALL        = size.small
NORMAL       = size.normal
ATR          = 'Atr'
RANGE        = 'Cumulative Mean Range'
CLOSE_SRC    = 'Close'
BODY_SRC     = 'Body'
HIGHLOW      = 'High/Low'
SOLID        = 'Solid'
DASHED       = 'Dashed'
DOTTED       = 'Dotted'
FULL_CANDLE  = 'Full Candle'
BODY_ONLY    = 'Body Only'

SMART_GROUP    = 'Smart Money Concepts'
INTERNAL_GROUP = 'Real Time Internal Structure'
SWING_GROUP    = 'Real Time Swing Structure'
BLOCKS_GROUP   = 'Order Blocks'
BREAKER_GROUP  = 'Breaker Blocks'
EQUAL_GROUP    = 'EQH/EQL'
GAPS_GROUP     = 'Fair Value Gaps'
LEVELS_GROUP   = 'Highs & Lows MTF'
ZONES_GROUP    = 'Premium & Discount Zones'
SWEEP_GROUP    = 'Liquidity Sweeps'
MSS_GROUP      = 'Market Structure Shift'
OTE_GROUP      = 'Optimal Trade Entry'
IFVG_GROUP     = 'Inverted Fair Value Gaps'
ASIANRANGE_GROUP = 'Asian Range'
IB_GROUP       = 'Initial Balance'
KILLZONE_GROUP = 'Kill Zones'
SESSION_GROUP  = 'Sessions'
PDHL_GROUP     = 'Previous Day / Week Levels'
NDOG_GROUP     = 'Opening Gaps (NDOG/NWOG)'
CVD_GROUP      = 'Cumulative Volume Delta (CVD)'
RVOL_GROUP     = 'Volume Validation (RVOL)'
VI_GROUP       = 'Volume Imbalance (VI)'
AVWAP_GROUP    = 'Anchored VWAP'

MAX_SESSION_BOXES  = 50
MAX_SESSION_LABELS = 50

MAX_ARRAY_SIZE       = 5000
MAX_STRUCTURE_LINES  = 200
MAX_STRUCTURE_LABELS = 200
MAX_SWING_LABELS     = 200
MAX_EQ_LINES         = 100
MAX_EQ_LABELS        = 100
MAX_ORDER_BLOCK_COUNT = 100
MAX_FVG_COUNT        = 100
MAX_BREAKER_COUNT    = 100
MAX_SWEEP_LABELS     = 100
MAX_EQ_POOLS         = 5

//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Inputs
//──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
modeInput                      = input.string(HISTORICAL, 'Mode',   group=SMART_GROUP, options=[HISTORICAL,PRESENT], display = display.none)
styleInput                     = input.string(COLORED,    'Style',  group=SMART_GROUP, options=[COLORED,MONOCHROME], display = display.none)
showTrendInput                 = input(false, 'Color Candles',       group=SMART_GROUP, display = display.none)
pivotSourceInput               = input.string('Body', 'Pivot Source', group=SMART_GROUP, options=['Body','Wick'], tooltip='Body = structure levels at candle bodies (filters wick sweeps from triggering BOS).\nWick = standard ICT swing definition (levels at actual highs/lows).', display = display.none)
showCEMidlinesInput            = input(true, 'Show CE Midlines (50%)', group=SMART_GROUP,
    tooltip='Draws a dotted midline at the 50% level (Consequent Encroachment) of Order Blocks and Breaker Blocks.\nFVG midpoint is already shown by the box split.\nThis is the optimal entry level in ICT methodology.', display = display.none)

showInternalsInput             = input(true,  'Show Internal Structure',   group=INTERNAL_GROUP, display = display.none)
showInternalBullInput          = input.string(ALL, 'Bullish Structure',    group=INTERNAL_GROUP, inline='ibull', options=[ALL,BOS,CHOCH], display = display.none)
internalBullColorInput         = input(GREEN, '',                          group=INTERNAL_GROUP, inline='ibull', display = display.none)
showInternalBearInput          = input.string(ALL, 'Bearish Structure',    group=INTERNAL_GROUP, inline='ibear', options=[ALL,BOS,CHOCH], display = display.none)
internalBearColorInput         = input(RED,   '',                          group=INTERNAL_GROUP, inline='ibear', display = display.none)
internalFilterConfluenceInput  = input(false, 'Confluence Filter',         group=INTERNAL_GROUP, display = display.none)
internalStructureSize          = input.string(TINY, 'Internal Label Size', group=INTERNAL_GROUP, options=[TINY,SMALL,NORMAL], display = display.none)
internalLengthInput            = input.int(5, 'Internal Swing Length',     group=INTERNAL_GROUP, minval=2, maxval=20, tooltip='Pivot lookback for internal structure.', display = display.none)

showStructureInput             = input(true,  'Show Swing Structure',      group=SWING_GROUP, display = display.none)
showSwingBullInput             = input.string(ALL, 'Bullish Structure',    group=SWING_GROUP, inline='bull', options=[ALL,BOS,CHOCH], display = display.none)
swingBullColorInput            = input(GREEN, '',                          group=SWING_GROUP, inline='bull', display = display.none)
showSwingBearInput             = input.string(ALL, 'Bearish Structure',    group=SWING_GROUP, inline='bear', options=[ALL,BOS,CHOCH], display = display.none)
swingBearColorInput            = input(RED,   '',                          group=SWING_GROUP, inline='bear', display = display.none)
swingStructureSize             = input.string(SMALL, 'Swing Label Size',   group=SWING_GROUP, options=[TINY,SMALL,NORMAL], display = display.none)
showSwingsInput                = input(false, 'Show Swing Points',         group=SWING_GROUP, inline='swings', display = display.none)
swingsLengthInput              = input.int(20, '',                         group=SWING_GROUP, minval=5, inline='swings', tooltip='Swing pivot lookback length.', display = display.none)
showHighLowSwingsInput         = input(true,  'Show Strong/Weak High/Low', group=SWING_GROUP, display = display.none)

showInternalOrderBlocksInput   = input(true,  'Internal Order Blocks',     group=BLOCKS_GROUP, inline='iob', display = display.none)
internalOrderBlocksSizeInput   = input.int(5, '',                          group=BLOCKS_GROUP, minval=1, maxval=20, inline='iob', display = display.none)
showSwingOrderBlocksInput      = input(false, 'Swing Order Blocks',        group=BLOCKS_GROUP, inline='ob', display = display.none)
swingOrderBlocksSizeInput      = input.int(5, '',                          group=BLOCKS_GROUP, minval=1, maxval=20, inline='ob', display = display.none)
orderBlockFilterInput          = input.string('Atr', 'OB Filter',          group=BLOCKS_GROUP, options=[ATR,RANGE], display = display.none)
orderBlockMitigationInput      = input.string(BODY_SRC, 'OB Mitigation',   group=BLOCKS_GROUP, options=[CLOSE_SRC,BODY_SRC,HIGHLOW],
    tooltip='Close = close must cross the OB level (strictest).\nBody = candle body must cross (ICT standard — filters wick sweeps).\nHigh/Low = any wick through the level counts (most aggressive).', display = display.none)
minPenetrationFactorInput      = input.float(0.1, 'Min Penetration xATR',  group=BLOCKS_GROUP, minval=0.0, maxval=1.0, step=0.05,
    tooltip='Minimum fraction of ATR required to penetrate the OB level for valid mitigation (filters marginal body clips).', display = display.none)
// v19.9 — Was hard-coded at 5 in the OB origin search. Exposed so users
//         on higher timeframes / longer consolidations can extend the
//         look-back when the actual OB candle is older than 100 bars.
//         Internal OB search keeps its fixed 3× multiplier (faster +
//         less back-history needed for internal structure).
obSearchCapMultiplierInput     = input.int(5, 'OB Search Multiplier (× Swing Length)', group=BLOCKS_GROUP, minval=2, maxval=15,
    tooltip='How far back the swing-OB origin scan looks (in multiples of Swing Length).\nDefault 5 = up to 100 bars at default Swing Length 20.\nHigher (8–15) = catches older OB origins on long consolidations or wide CHoCH legs; slightly slower.\nLower (2–4) = faster, may miss older origins.', display = display.none)
// v20.4 — Which end of the natural origin→broken window the search cap is
//         anchored to. Matters only when the window is LARGER than the cap.
//         'Origin' (legacy default) = scan forward from origin pivot up to
//         obSearchCap bars. Bars CLOSER TO BROKEN pivot can be cut off.
//         Aligns with "first opposite candle near the swing low/high" view.
//         'Break' = scan backward from broken pivot up to obSearchCap bars.
//         Bars CLOSER TO ORIGIN pivot can be cut off. Aligns with "last
//         opposite candle right before the structural break" view.
obSearchAnchorInput            = input.string('Origin', 'OB Search Anchor', group=BLOCKS_GROUP,
    options=['Origin','Break'],
    tooltip='PREFERENCE order when the impulse range exceeds the OB Search Multiplier cap. v20.6+ has a two-stage scan with automatic fallback, so neither setting can miss an OB anymore — the anchor only chooses which half of the range is searched FIRST:\n  Origin = scan near origin pivot first. If no opposite-color candle is found there, fall back to scanning near the broken pivot. OB tends to land near the swing low/high.\n  Break  = scan near broken pivot first. If no opposite-color candle is found there, fall back to scanning near origin. OB tends to land near the last pullback before the structural break.\nWhen the natural range fits within the cap, the full range is always scanned regardless of this setting.', display = display.none)
// v20.0 — Session-aware OB tagging. Each OB now stores which session
//         (Asian / London / NY / Off) it formed in. ICT lore: London OBs
//         and NY OBs behave differently — London tends to set the day's
//         direction, NY tends to reverse it. Optional visual: append the
//         session tag to the OB box text. Optional filter: only draw OBs
//         from a specific session.
showOBSessionTagInput          = input(false, 'Show OB Session Tag', group=BLOCKS_GROUP,
    tooltip='Appends the formation session (A/L/NY/Off) to the OB box text.\nUseful for confluence reading — London OBs often have different character than NY ones.', display = display.none)
obSessionFilterInput           = input.string('All', 'OB Session Filter', group=BLOCKS_GROUP,
    options=['All','Asian','London','NY','Off-Session'],
    tooltip='Show only OBs that formed during this session.\nAll = show all (default).\nDoes not affect breaker tracking or mitigation logic, only visual display.', display = display.none)
// v20.0 — OB confluence scoring. At formation, each OB gets a 0-3 score:
//           +1 if isInstitutional (high RVOL — requires RVOL stamping ON)
//           +1 if its price range overlaps any existing FVG
//           +1 if its midpoint sits in the top 30% (premium) or bottom 30%
//              (discount) of the current trailing-extreme range
//         When the score meets the threshold below, fires a
//         "High Confluence OB Formed" alert. Optional visual: append ★N
//         badge to the OB box text.
showOBConfluenceScoreInput     = input(false, 'Show OB Confluence Score', group=BLOCKS_GROUP,
    tooltip='Appends a ★N badge plus a letter breakdown to OB boxes, e.g. "★2 RF".\nN = total score (1-3). Letters show WHICH confluences scored:\n  R = institutional RVOL (requires RVOL stamping ON)\n  F = overlaps a Fair Value Gap\n  P = sits in the Premium/Discount zone (bullish OB in discount / bearish in premium)', display = display.none)
obConfluenceMinScoreInput      = input.int(3, 'High-Confluence OB Min Score', group=BLOCKS_GROUP, minval=1, maxval=3,
    tooltip='Minimum confluence score to fire the "High Confluence OB" alert.\n3 = strictest (must hit all three confluences).\n2 = looser. 1 = essentially any OB.\n\nDependencies — to reach score=3 you need all three feeders active:\n  • Institutional point requires RVOL stamping ON (Volume Validation group).\n  • FVG-overlap point requires FVG tracking ON (Fair Value Gaps group OR iFVG enabled — the FVG array must be populated).\n  • Premium/Discount point requires at least one BOS/CHoCH to have established trailing extremes, AND v20.1 makes this bias-aware (bullish OB in discount, bearish OB in premium).\nIf any feeder is off, the achievable max drops by 1.', display = display.none)
minPenetrationTicksInput       = input.float(0.0, 'Min Penetration Ticks', group=BLOCKS_GROUP, minval=0.0, step=1.0,
    tooltip='Absolute minimum tick penetration required (useful for low ATR conditions).', display = display.none)
orderBlockRangeInput           = input.string(FULL_CANDLE, 'OB Range',     group=BLOCKS_GROUP, options=[FULL_CANDLE,BODY_ONLY], tooltip='Full Candle = standard ICT (wicks included). Body Only = tighter zones.', display = display.none)
internalBullishOrderBlockColor = input.color(color.new(#3179f5,80), 'Internal Bull OB', group=BLOCKS_GROUP, display = display.none)
internalBearishOrderBlockColor = input.color(color.new(#f77c80,80), 'Internal Bear OB', group=BLOCKS_GROUP, display = display.none)
swingBullishOrderBlockColor    = input.color(color.new(#1848cc,80), 'Bullish OB',       group=BLOCKS_GROUP, display = display.none)
swingBearishOrderBlockColor    = input.color(color.new(#b22833,80), 'Bearish OB',       group=BLOCKS_GROUP, display = display.none)
showOBTouchCountInput          = input(true,  'Show Touch Count on OBs',   group=BLOCKS_GROUP, display = display.none)
maxOBTouchesInput              = input.int(3, 'Max Touches Before Exhaust', group=BLOCKS_GROUP,
    minval=1, maxval=10,
    tooltip='After this many discrete retests (outside→inside transitions), the Order Block (or Breaker Block) is removed as exhausted.\n1st touch = highest probability.', display = display.none)

showInternalBreakerBlocksInput   = input(false, 'Internal Breaker Blocks',  group=BREAKER_GROUP, inline='ibb', display = display.none)
internalBreakerBlocksSizeInput   = input.int(5, '',                         group=BREAKER_GROUP, minval=1, maxval=20, inline='ibb', display = display.none)
showSwingBreakerBlocksInput      = input(false, 'Swing Breaker Blocks',     group=BREAKER_GROUP, inline='bb', display = display.none)
swingBreakerBlocksSizeInput      = input.int(5, '',                         group=BREAKER_GROUP, minval=1, maxval=20, inline='bb',
     tooltip='When an Order Block is mitigated, it becomes a Breaker Block with flipped bias.\nBullish OB broken → Bearish Breaker (resistance)\nBearish OB broken → Bullish Breaker (support)\nOBs are tracked internally even if OB display is off.', display = display.none)
internalBullishBreakerColor      = input.color(color.new(#00bcd4,70), 'Internal Bull BB', group=BREAKER_GROUP, display = display.none)
internalBearishBreakerColor      = input.color(color.new(#ff9800,70), 'Internal Bear BB', group=BREAKER_GROUP, display = display.none)
swingBullishBreakerColor         = input.color(color.new(#00838f,70), 'Bullish BB',       group=BREAKER_GROUP, display = display.none)
swingBearishBreakerColor         = input.color(color.new(#e65100,70), 'Bearish BB',       group=BREAKER_GROUP, display = display.none)
showBBTouchCountInput            = input(true,  'Show Touch Count on BBs',  group=BREAKER_GROUP,
    tooltip='Display retest count on Breaker Blocks, independent of OB touch count toggle.', display = display.none)

showEqualHighsLowsInput        = input(true,   'Equal High/Low',           group=EQUAL_GROUP, display = display.none)
equalHighsLowsLengthInput      = input.int(3,  'EQH/EQL Pivot Length', group=EQUAL_GROUP, minval=1, maxval=50,
     tooltip='Pivot lookback for EQH/EQL detection only.\n' +
             'Independent from Swing Length (Real Time Swing Structure)\n' +
             'and Internal Swing Length (Real Time Internal Structure).\n' +
             'Default 3 = highly sensitive (many EQH/EQL labels).\n' +
             'Try 5–10 for fewer, higher-quality liquidity pools.', display = display.none)
equalHighsLowsThresholdInput   = input.float(0.1, 'Threshold (× ATR)',     group=EQUAL_GROUP, minval=0, maxval=0.5, step=0.1, display = display.none)
// v20.0 — Absolute-ticks floor for EQH/EQL tolerance. The ATR-based threshold
//         is fine for FX majors but produces too-loose tolerance on high-ATR
//         instruments like JPY pairs / index futures. The effective threshold
//         is now max(ATR_factor × ATR, ticks × mintick). Default 0 = ATR-only
//         (legacy behavior preserved). On NQ/ES try 50–200 ticks; on JPY
//         try 50–100 ticks.
equalHighsLowsTicksInput       = input.int(0, 'Threshold Floor (ticks)',  group=EQUAL_GROUP, minval=0, maxval=2000,
     tooltip='Absolute lower bound on the EQH/EQL tolerance, in ticks.\n0 = off (legacy ATR-only behavior).\nUseful on JPY pairs and index futures where 0.1×ATR is too wide.', display = display.none)
equalHighsLowsSizeInput        = input.string(TINY, 'Label Size',          group=EQUAL_GROUP, options=[TINY,SMALL,NORMAL], display = display.none)
// v18.8 — Optional freshness timeout. If > 0, an EQ match where the
//         previous EQ pivot is more than N bars old resets the streak
//         counter to 1. Defaults to 0 (disabled) to preserve cumulative
//         streak behavior. Use to suppress inflated EQH×N badges where
//         the touches span large time gaps.
eqMaxBarsBetweenMatchesInput   = input.int(0, 'Max Bars Between Matches', group=EQUAL_GROUP,
     minval=0, maxval=500,
     tooltip='If > 0, EQH/EQL matches more than this many bars after the\n' +
             'previous match still draw an EQH/EQL label but reset the\n' +
             'streak count to 1 (preventing inflated x N badges from\n' +
             'unrelated price visits to the same level long ago).\n' +
             'Default 0 = disabled.', display = display.none)
// v18.9 — Independent pivot source for EQH/EQL level comparison.
//         Affects only the EQ-comparison level, not pivot detection itself.
eqPivotComparisonInput         = input.string('Follow Main', 'EQH/EQL Pivot Source', group=EQUAL_GROUP,
     options=['Follow Main', 'Body', 'Wick'],
     tooltip='Override the global Pivot Source setting for EQH/EQL only.\n' +
             '"Follow Main" inherits the global setting.\n' +
             '"Wick" compares actual highs/lows — authentic ICT\n' +
             '       liquidity-pool detection (where stops sit).\n' +
             '"Body" compares body extremes — filters wick noise.\n' +
             'Note: pivot DETECTION still uses the main Pivot Source;\n' +
             'this only affects the level used for the EQ comparison.', display = display.none)

showFairValueGapsInput         = input(false, 'Fair Value Gaps',            group=GAPS_GROUP, display = display.none)
fairValueGapsThresholdInput    = input(true,  'Auto Threshold',             group=GAPS_GROUP, display = display.none)
fairValueGapsTimeframeInput    = input.timeframe('', 'Timeframe',           group=GAPS_GROUP, display = display.none)
fairValueGapsBullColorInput    = input.color(color.new(#00ff68,70), 'Bullish FVG', group=GAPS_GROUP, display = display.none)
fairValueGapsBearColorInput    = input.color(color.new(#ff0008,70), 'Bearish FVG', group=GAPS_GROUP, display = display.none)
fairValueGapsExtendInput       = input.int(1, 'Extend FVG',                group=GAPS_GROUP, minval=0, display = display.none)

showIFVGInput       = input(false, 'Show Inverted FVGs',       group=IFVG_GROUP,
    tooltip='When a FVG is fully mitigated, it flips bias and becomes an iFVG.\nBullish FVG filled → Bearish iFVG (resistance).\nBearish FVG filled → Bullish iFVG (support).', display = display.none)
ifvgBullColorInput  = input.color(color.new(#00bcd4, 75), 'Bullish iFVG', group=IFVG_GROUP, display = display.none)
ifvgBearColorInput  = input.color(color.new(#ff9800, 75), 'Bearish iFVG', group=IFVG_GROUP, display = display.none)
ifvgMaxCountInput   = input.int(10, 'Max iFVGs Shown',        group=IFVG_GROUP, minval=1, maxval=50, display = display.none)
ifvgMitigationInput = input.string(BODY_SRC, 'iFVG Mitigation', group=IFVG_GROUP, options=[CLOSE_SRC,BODY_SRC,HIGHLOW],
    tooltip='Close = close must invalidate the iFVG level.\nBody = candle body must invalidate the level.\nHigh/Low = any wick through the level invalidates it.', display = display.none)

showDailyLevelsInput           = input(false, 'Daily',   group=LEVELS_GROUP, inline='daily', display = display.none)
dailyLevelsStyleInput          = input.string(SOLID, '', group=LEVELS_GROUP, inline='daily',   options=[SOLID,DASHED,DOTTED], display = display.none)
dailyLevelsColorInput          = input(BLUE, '',         group=LEVELS_GROUP, inline='daily', display = display.none)
showWeeklyLevelsInput          = input(false, 'Weekly',  group=LEVELS_GROUP, inline='weekly', display = display.none)
weeklyLevelsStyleInput         = input.string(SOLID, '', group=LEVELS_GROUP, inline='weekly',  options=[SOLID,DASHED,DOTTED], display = display.none)
weeklyLevelsColorInput         = input(BLUE, '',         group=LEVELS_GROUP, inline='weekly', display = display.none)
showMonthlyLevelsInput         = input(false, 'Monthly', group=LEVELS_GROUP, inline='monthly', display = display.none)
monthlyLevelsStyleInput        = input.string(SOLID, '', group=LEVELS_GROUP, inline='monthly', options=[SOLID,DASHED,DOTTED], display = display.none)
monthlyLevelsColorInput        = input(BLUE, '',         group=LEVELS_GROUP, inline='monthly', display = display.none)

showPremiumDiscountZonesInput  = input(false, 'Premium/Discount Zones', group=ZONES_GROUP, display = display.none)
premiumZoneColorInput          = input.color(RED,   'Premium Zone',      group=ZONES_GROUP, display = display.none)
equilibriumZoneColorInput      = input.color(GRAY,  'Equilibrium Zone',  group=ZONES_GROUP, display = display.none)
discountZoneColorInput         = input.color(GREEN, 'Discount Zone',     group=ZONES_GROUP, display = display.none)
// v19.6 — Default flipped to true. The old default (OFF) caused trailing
//         extremes to ratchet monotonically between swing pivots — on
//         ranging or extended consolidations the Premium/Discount/OTE box
//         widened without bound and no longer reflected current structure.
//         ICT convention is for the zone to track the most recent leg, so
//         ON is the more sensible default. Toggle OFF if you prefer the
//         legacy wide-envelope behavior.
useTrailResetInput             = input(true, 'Reset Range on Trend Change', group=ZONES_GROUP,
    tooltip='ON (default) = tight OTE/zones — resets trailing top/bottom on swing trend flip so the box tracks the current leg.\nOFF = legacy wide expanding range (ratchets between pivots).\nAffects Premium/Discount Zones, OTE Zone, and Strong/Weak High/Low.', display = display.none)

showLiquiditySweepsInput       = input(false, 'Liquidity Sweeps',         group=SWEEP_GROUP, display = display.none)
sweepBullColorInput            = input.color(GREEN, 'Bullish Sweep Color', group=SWEEP_GROUP, display = display.none)
sweepBearColorInput            = input.color(RED,   'Bearish Sweep Color', group=SWEEP_GROUP, display = display.none)
sweepLabelSizeInput            = input.string(TINY, 'Sweep Label Size',    group=SWEEP_GROUP, options=[TINY,SMALL,NORMAL], display = display.none)
// v20.7 — Multi-level swing-sweep tracking (BS-2 fix). Pre-v20.7 only the
//         SINGLE most-recent swing high and swing low were watched for
//         sweeps — the moment a new pivot formed, the old level's latch was
//         reset and the old level was no longer monitored. But old untouched
//         swing highs/lows are the real stop magnets in ICT. This input sets
//         how many of the most recent UNSWEPT swing highs (and lows) to keep
//         under sweep surveillance simultaneously. 1 = legacy single-level
//         behavior. 5 (default) = watch the last 5 unswept highs and lows.
swingSweepLevelsInput          = input.int(5, 'Swing Levels Watched for Sweeps', group=SWEEP_GROUP, minval=1, maxval=10,
     tooltip='How many recent UNSWEPT swing highs / lows to monitor for liquidity sweeps at once.\n1 = legacy behavior (only the latest swing high + latest swing low).\n5 (default) = also watches older untouched swings that price may run later.\nA level leaves the watch list when it is swept (wick-through + close back) or cleanly broken (close beyond it).', display = display.none)

showMSSInput          = input(true,  'Identify MSS (Displacement CHoCH)', group=MSS_GROUP,
    tooltip='When a CHoCH is confirmed by a displacement candle (large body, minimal wicks, direction matches), it is labelled MSS instead of CHoCH.\nMSS = higher conviction reversal signal.', display = display.none)
mssATRMultInput       = input.float(1.0, 'Displacement ATR Multiplier',   group=MSS_GROUP,
    minval=0.3, maxval=3.0, step=0.1,
    tooltip='Breakout candle body must exceed this × ATR to qualify as displacement.\n1.0 = body at least as large as average range.\nLower = more MSS signals. Higher = stricter filter.', display = display.none)
mssBodyRatioInput     = input.float(0.5, 'Min Body/Range Ratio',          group=MSS_GROUP,
    minval=0.2, maxval=0.9, step=0.05,
    tooltip='Minimum ratio of candle body to total range.\n0.5 = body is at least half the candle.\nHigher = cleaner candles only (less wick).', display = display.none)
mssDisplacementLookbackInput = input.int(3, 'MSS Displacement Lookback', group=MSS_GROUP,
    minval=1, maxval=10,
    tooltip='Number of recent bars that can qualify a CHoCH as MSS.\n3 preserves the original behavior.', display = display.none)
// v20.7 — Displacement / structure-quality ATR length. Displacement and the
//         Weak/Medium/Strong quality score measure a SINGLE-bar event, but
//         pre-v20.7 they were compared against atrMeasure = ATR(200) — a slow
//         200-bar baseline that stays stale across volatility regimes (after
//         a contraction it's still inflated from the prior expansion, so real
//         displacement bars read as "Weak" / MSS won't trigger; after an
//         expansion the opposite). A shorter ATR tracks the regime you're
//         actually trading. Default 14 = responsive. Set to 200 to restore
//         exact pre-v20.7 behavior. This length feeds ONLY displacement +
//         quality; the EQ-tolerance and minPen floors keep using ATR(200)
//         for stability (see dispQualityATR below).
dispQualityATRLenInput = input.int(14, 'Displacement/Quality ATR Length', group=MSS_GROUP,
    minval=5, maxval=200,
    tooltip='ATR length used for MSS displacement sizing AND the BOS/CHoCH Weak/Medium/Strong quality score.\n14 (default) = responsive to current regime.\n200 = legacy behavior (slow, regime-stale).\nDoes NOT affect EQH/EQL tolerance or min-penetration, which stay on ATR(200).', display = display.none)
mssApplyInternalInput = input(true,  'Apply to Internal Structure',       group=MSS_GROUP, display = display.none)
mssApplySwingInput    = input(true,  'Apply to Swing Structure',          group=MSS_GROUP, display = display.none)
// v20.0 — Structure-quality filter. Computes a Weak/Medium/Strong score for
//         every BOS/CHoCH based on (a) how far the close penetrated the
//         broken level (in ATRs) and (b) the bar's body-to-range ratio.
//         The filter gates the alert AND optionally the structure label
//         draw. MSS is now treated as a specialized "Strong CHoCH" path
//         that always passes regardless of this filter.
structureMinQualityInput = input.string('All', 'Minimum Structure Quality', group=MSS_GROUP,
     options=['All','Medium+','Strong Only'],
     tooltip='Filters BOS/CHoCH alerts (and optionally labels) by computed strength:\n' +
             '  Strong  = displacement ≥ 1.0×ATR AND body/range ≥ 0.6\n' +
             '  Medium  = displacement ≥ 0.3×ATR OR  body/range ≥ 0.4\n' +
             '  Weak    = neither above\n' +
             'All       = no filtering (default).\nMedium+   = drop Weak.\nStrong Only = drop Weak AND Medium.\nMSS bars always pass (they\'re already strength-validated).', display = display.none)
showStructureQualityBadgeInput = input(false, 'Show Quality Badge on Structure Labels', group=MSS_GROUP,
     tooltip='Appends (S)/(M)/(W) to BOS/CHoCH labels so you can read strength at a glance.', display = display.none)
mssBullColorInput     = input.color(#00e676, 'Bullish MSS Color',         group=MSS_GROUP, display = display.none)
mssBearColorInput     = input.color(#ff1744, 'Bearish MSS Color',         group=MSS_GROUP, display = display.none)
showDisplacementInput = input(true, 'Highlight Displacement Candles', group=MSS_GROUP,
    tooltip='Places a marker on the candle whose displacement qualified the MSS.\nOnly appears when an MSS is confirmed.', display = display.none)

showOTEInput       = input(false, 'Show OTE Zone',              group=OTE_GROUP, display = display.none)
oteBullColorInput  = input.color(color.new(#00e676, 75), 'Bullish OTE', group=OTE_GROUP, display = display.none)
oteBearColorInput  = input.color(color.new(#ff1744, 75), 'Bearish OTE', group=OTE_GROUP, display = display.none)
showOTEFibsInput   = input(true,  'Show Fib Lines (50% / 61.8% / 78.6%)', group=OTE_GROUP,
    tooltip='OTE = 61.8%–78.6% Fibonacci retracement of the current swing range.\nBullish trend → buy zone in discount.\nBearish trend → sell zone in premium.', display = display.none)
oteFib1Input       = input.float(0.618, 'Fib Level 1 (Upper)', group=OTE_GROUP, minval=0.5, maxval=0.9, step=0.01, display = display.none)
oteFib2Input       = input.float(0.786, 'Fib Level 2 (Lower)', group=OTE_GROUP, minval=0.5, maxval=0.95, step=0.01, display = display.none)
// v20.8 — OTE anchor mode (BS audit #1/#2/#3 fix).
//   Dealing Range (legacy default) — OTE fibs are measured off
//     trailing.top / trailing.bottom, the SAME envelope that drives the
//     Premium/Discount zone. That envelope keeps expanding as the trend
//     extends (every new body-high/low widens it), so the OTE band drifts
//     bar-to-bar and, on long trends, becomes the retracement of the whole
//     run rather than the last impulse leg. Kept as default for backward
//     compatibility.
//   Impulse Leg (correct ICT) — at the swing BOS/CHoCH/MSS that sets the
//     current bias, the originating leg (swing-low→break for bullish,
//     swing-high→break for bearish) is captured and FROZEN. The fib levels
//     then stay static (a placeable level, not a drifting zone) and the
//     zone is VOIDED when price closes beyond the leg origin — so a long
//     whose origin gets violated stops showing "OTE Buy" instead of
//     stretching to chase price.
oteAnchorModeInput = input.string('Dealing Range', 'OTE Anchor', group=OTE_GROUP,
    options=['Dealing Range','Impulse Leg'],
    tooltip='Dealing Range (legacy) = OTE measured off the Premium/Discount envelope; drifts as the trend extends.\nImpulse Leg (ICT-correct) = OTE frozen to the last impulse leg at the BOS/MSS that set bias; static fib levels, and the zone is voided when price closes beyond the leg origin.', display = display.none)

showAsianRangeInput      = input(false, 'Show Asian Range H/L',  group=ASIANRANGE_GROUP, display = display.none)
asianRangeSessionInput   = input.string('2000-0000', 'Session Hours', group=ASIANRANGE_GROUP,
    options=['1800-0000','1900-0000','2000-0000','2000-0100','2100-0200'],
    tooltip='Asian session hours in HHMM-HHMM format.\n2000-0000 = 20:00 to 00:00.\nAll times in the selected timezone.', display = display.none)
rangeTimezoneInput  = input.string('America/New_York', 'Range Timezone', group=ASIANRANGE_GROUP,
    options=['America/New_York','America/Chicago','America/Los_Angeles',
            'Europe/London','Europe/Berlin','Asia/Tokyo','Asia/Hong_Kong',
            'Asia/Kolkata','Asia/Singapore','Australia/Sydney','UTC'], display = display.none)
asianRangeHighColorInput = input.color(color.new(#e040fb, 30), 'Asian High Color', group=ASIANRANGE_GROUP, display = display.none)
asianRangeLowColorInput  = input.color(color.new(#e040fb, 30), 'Asian Low Color',  group=ASIANRANGE_GROUP, display = display.none)
asianRangeStyleInput     = input.string(DASHED, 'Line Style',    group=ASIANRANGE_GROUP, options=[SOLID,DASHED,DOTTED], display = display.none)

